/*!
  \page example_sycl_basic_page Fitting in SYCL kernels

  This example fits a plane (Ponca::MeanPlaneFit) at every point of a planar point cloud in a SYCL kernel: the points
  are copied to device memory, and each work-item of a `parallel_for` iterates over all the points to compute the
  potential of the fitted plane at its point.

  The example is compiled when <a href="https://adaptivecpp.github.io/" target="_blank">AdaptiveCpp</a> is found by
  CMake:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_basic_sycl
  ./build/examples/sycl/ponca_basic_sycl
  \endcode

  See also \ref ponca_gpu_sycl.

  \include sycl/ponca_basic_sycl.cpp
*/
